Gene prediction and annotation
Besides other bioinformatics analyses, the most significant analysis of this study was the prediction of bacterial genes involved in plastic degradation. The contigs were subjected to Prokka v1.13 for genes prediction that were annotated using EggNOG-mapper v2.0.1 based on EggNOG database v5.0. The EggNOG database is a hierarchical, functionally, and phylogenetically annotated orthology resource. Like the COG database, genes are categorized into 25 categories (Alneberg et al. 2014; Lenfant et al. 2013; Seemann 2014).
Enrichment of alpha and beta hydrolases
Alignment of predicted coding sequences (pCDS) from the metagenome sample was carried out against the ESTHER database of alpha/beta hydrolases (depolymerases, esterases, lipases, and cutinases) that were also reported for plastic degradation previously (DiGiacomo et al. 2022). CD-HIT version 4.7 was used to cluster protein sequences with default settings to reduce redundancy within the database. The modified database used included 10 protein families containing a total of 17,312 protein sequences. Alignments were performed using the command-line version of
